    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7442" root="حذفر" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُذْفُورٌ</span></b> : see above, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>A
numerous congregation</i> or <i>assemblage.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
And <i>An eminent, an elevated,</i> or <i>a noble, man:</i>
(K, TA:) pl. as above. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And the pl.,
(as some say, TA,) <i>Persons prepared for war.</i>
(K.) Whence the phrase, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اُشْدُدْ حَذَا فِيرَكَ</span> <i>Prepare
thyself</i> (K, TA) <i>for war, &amp;c.</i> (TA.)

